Same 8 cold solves as logs/default_strategy_nondeterminism, with
cudss_deterministic=true (CUDSS_CONFIG_DETERMINISTIC_MODE). Confirm via the
'cuDSS solve mode            : deterministic' line in each log.

Deterministic mode does NOT make the solve reproducible:
  - 6/8 converge in exactly 24 iterations (was a 24-27 spread without it)
  - 2/8 still break down and report 'Suboptimal solution found' at 31 iterations
  - objectives still differ across runs at ~1e-13

Why: at iteration 24 the dual infeasibility sits on the 1e-8 tolerance.
  run1 reaches 9.53e-09, passes, and stops at 24 iterations.
  run0 reaches 1.01e-08, fails, continues, and the dual residual then
  diverges to 1.68e-06 by iteration 27 and never recovers.
A last-digit difference decides which side of the tolerance you land on.

NOTE: this batch ran with all 8 GPUs at 100% from an unrelated job, so the
wall times (~8-10s) are contended and not comparable to the other batch.


